# apps/web TypeScript project structure

Source of truth: `.agents/skills/typescript-project-structure/SKILL.md`

## Must

- Keep application source under `apps/web/src/` only (Vite root may hold `index.html`, `vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `public/`).
- Place shared UI by role: `components/core/`, `components/patterns/`, `components/containers/` (when needed), `components/layouts/`.
- Use folder-per-component: `index.tsx` plus `index.types.ts` when props/types exist.
- Put section screens under `src/pages/<PageName>/`.
- Put URL routing under `src/routes/` (React Router). Do not reintroduce `useState` page switching in `App`.
- Import shared components by direct path (e.g. `@/components/core/CopyButton`). No component-layer barrel files.

## Must not

- Create empty unused folders (`contexts/`, `services/`, `stores/`, `i18n/`, `assets/`) until needed.
- Add `components/*/index.ts` re-export barrels.
- Put page screens back under `components/pages/` or `components/common/`.

## Styling

- MUI `sx` and `styles/theme.ts` are allowed. Do not add empty `index.module.css` files solely to satisfy the skill checklist.
